Article 20. Rights and Interests in the Family

Women have rights and interests in the family as follows:

•	When the wife is pregnant or when the newly born child is less than one year old, the husband is not allowed to request a divorce. However, the wife has the right to do so;
•	In the event of divorce, the wife has priority regarding custody of the children;
•	If sexual relations occur between a man and a woman and if [either] the man does not marry the woman or they have a child before marriage, the woman shall be entitled to claim compensation from the man and she shall also have the right to request for expenses for child care until the child reaches 18 years of age11;
•	In the event of the division of an inheritance, a mother has the right to represent her unborn child to inherit and manage such inheritance.

